A novel merging of the renormalization group with gradient descent techniques,
known as GDPRG, has been developed to precisely determine the renormalization group
flow of quantum field theories. This merged approach is demonstrated to be effective
in two examples: (one) non-gaussian quantum field theories with a simple renormalization group
operator and (two) various gaussian theories with a general renormalization group operator. 
Furthermore, GDPRG is shown to be an efficient method for the renormalization group
flow of theories with a simple phase transition while facing challenges in theories with
complex phase transitions. This approach is anticipated to be instrumental in studying
the renormalization group flow of various quantum field theories. 

